-- ISSUE-HYGIENE-1 (2026-10-26, pillar autonomy; owner question: "are there duplicate, deprecated or obsolete issues that need to be cleaned up? what about old issues?")
--
-- WHAT WAS MEASURED (qnfo-audit SELECT only, GitHub list reads, 2026-10-26 06:00-07:30Z)
--   438 open agent_issues (GitHub mirrors them 1:1 through TRACKER-SYNC-1). 149 were opened and 135 closed in the last 24 hours (drain ratio 0.91,
--   target 1.5). The inflow is dominated by tickets ABOUT other records, not by defects:
--     PROBE-NEEDED-1   75 opened in 7 days, 53 open: an issue per orphan that has no probe (REOPEN-LIVE-PATH-3). 5 of the 53 name a target that is already
--                      closed, and their contracts sit in probe-review-refused, which takes them out of the auto-close path, so nothing ever closes them.
--     CODE-MERGE-REFUSED-1  all 10 open ones name a code task that has since MERGED (code_tasks.status = merged); the filer never closes on merge.
--     CODE-LOOP-EXHAUSTED-1 15 open; the issue's own definition of done is "the task, or a task that replaces it, reaches ready_to_publish": 7 are met
--                      (the issue the task worked is closed, or a replacement task is merged); the other 8 are real escalations and stay.
--     [self-heal] tool X failing xN (...)  10 open copies, NULL source: qnfo-observability evReview copies each qnfo-ops ledger row into agent_issues
--                      keyed by the ledger TITLE, which embeds a changing count, so every count change files a new issue, and nothing closes it when the
--                      ledger row resolves; every one of the 10 ledger rows is resolved (last seen 2026-10-24 to 2026-10-25).
--     OWNER-TASK-op-* 63 open: the owner pressed the same dashboard "Fix" button again, and the intake (OWNER-NOTES-ROUTE-1) dedupes by whole title while
--                      every title carries its own op id. 10 are whole-prompt twins of an older open ticket, 7 more are the same objective in other words
--                      (read in full), 5 ask for the fix of an issue that is already closed with verified evidence.
--     STALE-PR-CHECK-REPAIR-1  3 open for PRs 3931, 3935 and 3941, all merged on 2026-10-25.
--
-- WHAT THIS CHANGES
--   Every rule below closes an issue only on a fact it reads in the same statement and writes into the evidence. Nothing is deleted, nothing is wontfix,
--   no open ticket that carries work is touched. For every issue it closes:
--     1. issue_fold_ledger saves the before-state first (status, close channel, triage row, contract), one row per close, applied = 0 until it is done;
--     2. its contract (status monitoring, superseded, probe-review-refused ...) is set to superseded, so close-while-contract-fails cannot abort the set;
--     3. its close_channel is 'workflow:ISSUE-HYGIENE-1 <rule>' (CLOSE-CHANNEL-REQUIRED-1);
--     4. its issue_triage row is closed with the evidence ("moot: ..." or "superseded by <id> ..."); the live trigger triage_close_sync_issue_upd closes the
--        issue and issue_lifecycle_au writes 'dispositioned' with has_evidence 1 (v_issue_accounting counts it as closed with disposition);
--     5. the ledger row is marked applied once the issue is out of 'open'.
--   The six rules that read live state (probe-needed-target-not-open, code-merge-refused-task-merged, code-loop-exhausted-dod-met, ledger-escalation-resolved,
--   owner-task-names-closed-issue, owner-prompt-twin) are also the hourly workflow issue-meta-fold (fleet_tasks + fleet_crons, :20 each hour), so a ticket
--   about a record closes within the hour of that record's resolution instead of waiting for a person. Two rules run once, here: a merged-PR fact read from
--   GitHub on 2026-10-26 (PRs 3931, 3935, 3941) and seven same-objective pairs read in full by hand (Errata chain, D1 truncation fix, desktop-client cost).
--
-- NOT ADDED (stated): no trigger and no unique index on agent_issues or issue_triage (AGENT-ISSUES-TRIGGER-DEPTH-1, migrations/2026-10-19-metric-twin-supersede.sql
-- records the 10-level D1 limit and the 2026-10-18 outage). Prevention is the hourly workflow plus a detector (fm-meta-issue-outlives-subject) plus the
-- code fixes that stop the producers: qnfo-observability dedupes its escalation by ledger fingerprint (a separate pull request) and the dashboard intake links
-- a repeated owner prompt to the open ticket (code task filed, qnfo-fleet-dashboard/worker.js is claimed by another session at the time of writing).
--
-- Revert: restore status, close channel, triage and contract from issue_fold_ledger (the Rollback line does it for every applied row); the workflow is
-- disabled with UPDATE fleet_crons SET enabled = 0 WHERE name = 'issue-meta-fold-hourly'.
--
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- Rollback: UPDATE issue_triage SET triage_state = (SELECT f.triage_state FROM issue_fold_ledger f WHERE f.issue_id = issue_triage.issue_id AND f.applied = 1 ORDER BY f.id DESC LIMIT 1), close_evidence = (SELECT f.triage_close_evidence FROM issue_fold_ledger f WHERE f.issue_id = issue_triage.issue_id AND f.applied = 1 ORDER BY f.id DESC LIMIT 1), reopened_count = (SELECT f.triage_reopened_count FROM issue_fold_ledger f WHERE f.issue_id = issue_triage.issue_id AND f.applied = 1 ORDER BY f.id DESC LIMIT 1), triaged_at = (SELECT f.triage_triaged_at FROM issue_fold_ledger f WHERE f.issue_id = issue_triage.issue_id AND f.applied = 1 ORDER BY f.id DESC LIMIT 1) WHERE issue_id IN (SELECT issue_id FROM issue_fold_ledger WHERE applied = 1); UPDATE agent_issues SET status = 'open', close_channel = (SELECT f.agent_close_channel FROM issue_fold_ledger f WHERE f.issue_id = agent_issues.id AND f.applied = 1 ORDER BY f.id DESC LIMIT 1), updated_at = CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000 WHERE id IN (SELECT issue_id FROM issue_fold_ledger WHERE applied = 1) AND status = 'closed' AND close_channel LIKE 'workflow:ISSUE-HYGIENE-1%'; UPDATE remediation_contracts SET status = (SELECT f.contract_status FROM issue_fold_ledger f WHERE f.contract_class = remediation_contracts.class AND f.applied = 1 ORDER BY f.id DESC LIMIT 1), last_verdict = (SELECT f.contract_last_verdict FROM issue_fold_ledger f WHERE f.contract_class = remediation_contracts.class AND f.applied = 1 ORDER BY f.id DESC LIMIT 1) WHERE class IN (SELECT contract_class FROM issue_fold_ledger WHERE applied = 1 AND contract_class IS NOT NULL) AND last_verdict LIKE 'superseded:closure-superseded%'; UPDATE fleet_crons SET enabled = 0 WHERE name = 'issue-meta-fold-hourly'; DELETE FROM remediation_contracts WHERE class = 'fm-meta-issue-outlives-subject'; DELETE FROM failure_modes WHERE fm_key = 'meta-issue-outlives-subject'
--
-- Verify after apply:
--   SELECT rule, COUNT(*) FROM issue_fold_ledger GROUP BY rule;                                      -- 57 rows on the first apply: probe-needed 5, merge-refused 10, exhausted 7, ledger 10, owner-closed 5, owner-twin 10, stale-pr 3, semantic 7
--   SELECT COUNT(*) FROM issue_fold_ledger WHERE applied = 0;                                        -- 0
--   SELECT COUNT(*) FROM agent_issues WHERE status = 'open';                                         -- 438 - 57 or fewer
--   SELECT COUNT(*) FROM v_issue_accounting WHERE closed_without_disposition > 0;                    -- unchanged (every close has evidence)
--   SELECT last_fired FROM fleet_crons WHERE name = 'issue-meta-fold-hourly';                        -- within the hour

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS issue_fold_ledger (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, issue_id INTEGER NOT NULL, rule TEXT NOT NULL, successor_id INTEGER, evidence TEXT NOT NULL,
  agent_status TEXT, agent_updated_at INTEGER, agent_close_channel TEXT, triage_state TEXT, triage_close_evidence TEXT, triage_reopened_count INTEGER, triage_triaged_at TEXT,
  contract_class TEXT, contract_status TEXT, contract_last_verdict TEXT, contract_last_attempt_at TEXT,
  applied INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0, created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (datetime('now')), applied_at TEXT);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_issue_fold_ledger_issue ON issue_fold_ledger(issue_id, applied);

-- 1. The rules that read live state (also the hourly workflow); each fills the ledger with the before-state and the evidence
INSERT INTO issue_fold_ledger (issue_id, rule, successor_id, evidence, agent_status, agent_updated_at, agent_close_channel, triage_state, triage_close_evidence, triage_reopened_count, triage_triaged_at, contract_class, contract_status, contract_last_verdict, contract_last_attempt_at) SELECT m.id, 'probe-needed-target-not-open', x.id, 'moot: issue ' || x.id || ' is ' || x.status || ' (' || substr(x.title, 1, 80) || '): the probe this issue asked for belongs to a target that no longer needs one, so the to-do outlived its subject. ISSUE-HYGIENE-1 ' || strftime('%Y-%m-%d', 'now'), m.status, m.updated_at, m.close_channel, t.triage_state, t.close_evidence, t.reopened_count, t.triaged_at, c.class, c.status, c.last_verdict, c.last_attempt_at FROM agent_issues m JOIN issue_triage t ON t.issue_id = m.id LEFT JOIN remediation_contracts c ON c.class = 'issue-' || m.id JOIN agent_issues x ON x.id = CAST(substr(m.title, 23) AS INTEGER) WHERE m.status = 'open' AND m.title GLOB 'PROBE-NEEDED-1: issue-[0-9]*' AND x.status <> 'open' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_fold_ledger f WHERE f.issue_id = m.id AND f.applied = 0) ORDER BY m.id LIMIT 200;
INSERT INTO issue_fold_ledger (issue_id, rule, successor_id, evidence, agent_status, agent_updated_at, agent_close_channel, triage_state, triage_close_evidence, triage_reopened_count, triage_triaged_at, contract_class, contract_status, contract_last_verdict, contract_last_attempt_at) SELECT m.id, 'code-merge-refused-task-merged', NULL, 'moot: code task ' || k.id || ' is merged (code_tasks.status, last updated ' || COALESCE(k.updated_at, '?') || '), so the merge refusal this issue recorded no longer holds. ISSUE-HYGIENE-1 ' || strftime('%Y-%m-%d', 'now'), m.status, m.updated_at, m.close_channel, t.triage_state, t.close_evidence, t.reopened_count, t.triaged_at, c.class, c.status, c.last_verdict, c.last_attempt_at FROM agent_issues m JOIN issue_triage t ON t.issue_id = m.id LEFT JOIN remediation_contracts c ON c.class = 'issue-' || m.id JOIN code_tasks k ON k.id = substr(m.title, 33, instr(substr(m.title, 33) || ' ', ' ') - 1) WHERE m.status = 'open' AND m.title LIKE 'CODE-MERGE-REFUSED-1: code task ct_%' AND k.status = 'merged' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_fold_ledger f WHERE f.issue_id = m.id AND f.applied = 0) ORDER BY m.id LIMIT 200;
INSERT INTO issue_fold_ledger (issue_id, rule, successor_id, evidence, agent_status, agent_updated_at, agent_close_channel, triage_state, triage_close_evidence, triage_reopened_count, triage_triaged_at, contract_class, contract_status, contract_last_verdict, contract_last_attempt_at) SELECT m.id, 'code-loop-exhausted-dod-met', r.id, 'moot: the definition of done of this issue (the task or a task that replaces it reaches ready_to_publish or later) is met: ' || CASE WHEN r.status IN ('closed', 'resolved') THEN 'issue ' || r.id || ' (' || substr(r.title, 1, 70) || ') is ' || r.status ELSE 'a replacement task for issue ' || r.id || ' is merged or published' END || '. ISSUE-HYGIENE-1 ' || strftime('%Y-%m-%d', 'now'), m.status, m.updated_at, m.close_channel, t.triage_state, t.close_evidence, t.reopened_count, t.triaged_at, c.class, c.status, c.last_verdict, c.last_attempt_at FROM agent_issues m JOIN issue_triage t ON t.issue_id = m.id LEFT JOIN remediation_contracts c ON c.class = 'issue-' || m.id JOIN code_tasks k ON k.id = substr(m.title, 24, instr(substr(m.title, 24) || ' ', ' ') - 1) JOIN agent_issues r ON r.id = CASE WHEN k.id LIKE 'ct_im%' THEN CAST(substr(k.id, 6) AS INTEGER) WHEN k.goal LIKE '[issue #%' THEN CAST(substr(k.goal, 9) AS INTEGER) END WHERE m.status = 'open' AND m.title LIKE 'CODE-LOOP-EXHAUSTED-1: ct_%' AND (r.status IN ('closed', 'resolved') OR EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM code_tasks k2 WHERE k2.id <> k.id AND k2.status IN ('merged', 'published') AND (k2.id = 'ct_im' || r.id OR instr(k2.goal, '[issue #' || r.id || ']') > 0))) AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_fold_ledger f WHERE f.issue_id = m.id AND f.applied = 0) ORDER BY m.id LIMIT 200;
INSERT INTO issue_fold_ledger (issue_id, rule, successor_id, evidence, agent_status, agent_updated_at, agent_close_channel, triage_state, triage_close_evidence, triage_reopened_count, triage_triaged_at, contract_class, contract_status, contract_last_verdict, contract_last_attempt_at) SELECT m.id, 'ledger-escalation-resolved', NULL, 'moot: the filing loop resolved its own ledger row (fingerprint ' || (SELECT l.fingerprint FROM issue_ledger l WHERE (l.title = m.title OR (m.title LIKE '[self-heal] tool %' AND l.title LIKE '[self-heal] tool %' AND substr(l.title, 18, instr(substr(l.title, 18) || ' ', ' ') - 1) = substr(m.title, 18, instr(substr(m.title, 18) || ' ', ' ') - 1))) AND l.status IN ('resolved', 'muted') ORDER BY l.last_seen DESC LIMIT 1) || ', last seen ' || (SELECT l.last_seen FROM issue_ledger l WHERE (l.title = m.title OR (m.title LIKE '[self-heal] tool %' AND l.title LIKE '[self-heal] tool %' AND substr(l.title, 18, instr(substr(l.title, 18) || ' ', ' ') - 1) = substr(m.title, 18, instr(substr(m.title, 18) || ' ', ' ') - 1))) AND l.status IN ('resolved', 'muted') ORDER BY l.last_seen DESC LIMIT 1) || ') and no open ledger row remains for it, so this escalation copy has nothing left to track. ISSUE-HYGIENE-1 ' || strftime('%Y-%m-%d', 'now'), m.status, m.updated_at, m.close_channel, t.triage_state, t.close_evidence, t.reopened_count, t.triaged_at, c.class, c.status, c.last_verdict, c.last_attempt_at FROM agent_issues m JOIN issue_triage t ON t.issue_id = m.id LEFT JOIN remediation_contracts c ON c.class = 'issue-' || m.id WHERE m.status = 'open' AND instr(COALESCE(m.description, ''), 'AUTO-ESCALATION from evReview') = 1 AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_ledger l WHERE (l.title = m.title OR (m.title LIKE '[self-heal] tool %' AND l.title LIKE '[self-heal] tool %' AND substr(l.title, 18, instr(substr(l.title, 18) || ' ', ' ') - 1) = substr(m.title, 18, instr(substr(m.title, 18) || ' ', ' ') - 1))) AND l.status IN ('resolved', 'muted')) AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_ledger l WHERE (l.title = m.title OR (m.title LIKE '[self-heal] tool %' AND l.title LIKE '[self-heal] tool %' AND substr(l.title, 18, instr(substr(l.title, 18) || ' ', ' ') - 1) = substr(m.title, 18, instr(substr(m.title, 18) || ' ', ' ') - 1))) AND l.status IN ('open', 'acknowledged')) AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_fold_ledger f WHERE f.issue_id = m.id AND f.applied = 0) ORDER BY m.id LIMIT 200;
INSERT INTO issue_fold_ledger (issue_id, rule, successor_id, evidence, agent_status, agent_updated_at, agent_close_channel, triage_state, triage_close_evidence, triage_reopened_count, triage_triaged_at, contract_class, contract_status, contract_last_verdict, contract_last_attempt_at) SELECT m.id, 'owner-task-names-closed-issue', r.id, 'moot: the task asks for the fix of issue ' || r.id || ' (' || substr(r.title, 1, 70) || '), which is ' || r.status || ' with close evidence: ' || substr(COALESCE((SELECT x.close_evidence FROM issue_triage x WHERE x.issue_id = r.id), '(none recorded)'), 1, 160) || ' ISSUE-HYGIENE-1 ' || strftime('%Y-%m-%d', 'now'), m.status, m.updated_at, m.close_channel, t.triage_state, t.close_evidence, t.reopened_count, t.triaged_at, c.class, c.status, c.last_verdict, c.last_attempt_at FROM agent_issues m JOIN issue_triage t ON t.issue_id = m.id LEFT JOIN remediation_contracts c ON c.class = 'issue-' || m.id JOIN agent_issues r ON r.id = CAST(substr(m.title, instr(m.title, '(issue #') + 8) AS INTEGER) WHERE m.status = 'open' AND m.source = 'qnfo-fleet-dashboard:owner-request' AND m.title LIKE 'OWNER-TASK-op-%' AND instr(m.title, '(issue #') > 0 AND r.id <> m.id AND r.status IN ('closed', 'resolved') AND instr(m.title, substr(r.title, 1, MIN(30, instr(r.title || ':', ':') - 1))) > 0 AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_fold_ledger f WHERE f.issue_id = m.id AND f.applied = 0) ORDER BY m.id LIMIT 200;
INSERT INTO issue_fold_ledger (issue_id, rule, successor_id, evidence, agent_status, agent_updated_at, agent_close_channel, triage_state, triage_close_evidence, triage_reopened_count, triage_triaged_at, contract_class, contract_status, contract_last_verdict, contract_last_attempt_at) SELECT m.id, 'owner-prompt-twin', s.id, 'superseded by ' || s.id || ' (' || substr(s.title, 1, 100) || ', open): the same owner prompt filed again, because the dashboard intake dedupes by whole title and every title carries its own op id. The older ticket carries the work. ISSUE-HYGIENE-1 ' || strftime('%Y-%m-%d', 'now'), m.status, m.updated_at, m.close_channel, t.triage_state, t.close_evidence, t.reopened_count, t.triaged_at, c.class, c.status, c.last_verdict, c.last_attempt_at FROM agent_issues m JOIN issue_triage t ON t.issue_id = m.id LEFT JOIN remediation_contracts c ON c.class = 'issue-' || m.id JOIN agent_issues s ON s.id = (SELECT MIN(o.id) FROM agent_issues o WHERE o.status = 'open' AND o.id < m.id AND o.source = m.source AND (o.title LIKE 'OWNER-TASK-op-%' OR o.title LIKE 'OWNER-NOTE-%') AND lower(trim(substr(o.title, instr(o.title, ': ') + 2))) = lower(trim(substr(m.title, instr(m.title, ': ') + 2)))) WHERE m.status = 'open' AND m.source = 'qnfo-fleet-dashboard:owner-request' AND (m.title LIKE 'OWNER-TASK-op-%' OR m.title LIKE 'OWNER-NOTE-%') AND instr(m.title, ': ') > 0 AND length(lower(trim(substr(m.title, instr(m.title, ': ') + 2)))) >= 20 AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_fold_ledger f WHERE f.issue_id = m.id AND f.applied = 0) ORDER BY m.id LIMIT 200;

-- 2. The rules that run once: a merged-PR fact read from GitHub on 2026-10-26, and seven same-objective pairs read in full
INSERT INTO issue_fold_ledger (issue_id, rule, successor_id, evidence, agent_status, agent_updated_at, agent_close_channel, triage_state, triage_close_evidence, triage_reopened_count, triage_triaged_at, contract_class, contract_status, contract_last_verdict, contract_last_attempt_at) SELECT m.id, 'stale-pr-check-repair-pr-merged', NULL, 'moot: PR ' || substr(m.title, 28, 4) || ' is merged (GitHub read ' || strftime('%Y-%m-%d', 'now') || ': state closed, merged true, merged_at ' || CASE substr(m.title, 28, 4) WHEN '3931' THEN '2026-10-25T07:10:17Z' WHEN '3935' THEN '2026-10-25T07:10:31Z' ELSE '2026-10-25T07:36:45Z' END || ', merged_by rwnq8), so the check repair this issue asked the lane for has nothing left to repair. ISSUE-HYGIENE-1 ' || strftime('%Y-%m-%d', 'now'), m.status, m.updated_at, m.close_channel, t.triage_state, t.close_evidence, t.reopened_count, t.triaged_at, c.class, c.status, c.last_verdict, c.last_attempt_at FROM agent_issues m JOIN issue_triage t ON t.issue_id = m.id LEFT JOIN remediation_contracts c ON c.class = 'issue-' || m.id WHERE m.status = 'open' AND (m.title LIKE 'STALE-PR-CHECK-REPAIR-1 PR 3931:%' OR m.title LIKE 'STALE-PR-CHECK-REPAIR-1 PR 3935:%' OR m.title LIKE 'STALE-PR-CHECK-REPAIR-1 PR 3941:%') AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_fold_ledger f WHERE f.issue_id = m.id AND f.applied = 0) ORDER BY m.id LIMIT 200;
INSERT INTO issue_fold_ledger (issue_id, rule, successor_id, evidence, agent_status, agent_updated_at, agent_close_channel, triage_state, triage_close_evidence, triage_reopened_count, triage_triaged_at, contract_class, contract_status, contract_last_verdict, contract_last_attempt_at) SELECT m.id, 'owner-task-semantic-twin', s.id, 'superseded by ' || s.id || ' (' || substr(s.title, 1, 100) || ', open): the same objective filed again in other words (read in full on 2026-10-26: the Errata watch/respond/publish chain stuck, the D1 truncation fix that makes DOIs the canonical full text, the untagged owner-local desktop client cost). The older ticket carries the work. ISSUE-HYGIENE-1 2026-10-26', m.status, m.updated_at, m.close_channel, t.triage_state, t.close_evidence, t.reopened_count, t.triaged_at, c.class, c.status, c.last_verdict, c.last_attempt_at FROM agent_issues m JOIN issue_triage t ON t.issue_id = m.id LEFT JOIN remediation_contracts c ON c.class = 'issue-' || m.id JOIN agent_issues s ON s.id = CASE m.id WHEN 1000073 THEN 1000064 WHEN 1000076 THEN 1000064 WHEN 1000081 THEN 1000064 WHEN 100585 THEN 100523 WHEN 100597 THEN 100523 WHEN 1000241 THEN 100523 WHEN 100385 THEN 100384 END AND s.status = 'open' WHERE m.status = 'open' AND m.id IN (1000073, 1000076, 1000081, 100585, 100597, 1000241, 100385) AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_fold_ledger f WHERE f.issue_id = m.id AND f.applied = 0) ORDER BY m.id LIMIT 200;

-- 3. Settle the contracts, name the channel, close through the triage row, mark the ledger
UPDATE remediation_contracts SET status = 'superseded', last_verdict = 'superseded:closure-superseded (ISSUE-HYGIENE-1)', last_attempt_at = datetime('now') WHERE class IN (SELECT f.contract_class FROM issue_fold_ledger f WHERE f.applied = 0 AND f.contract_class IS NOT NULL) AND status IN ('monitoring', 'escalated', 'active', 'holding', 'needs-machine-probe', 'probe-review-refused');
UPDATE agent_issues SET close_channel = 'workflow:ISSUE-HYGIENE-1 ' || (SELECT f.rule FROM issue_fold_ledger f WHERE f.issue_id = agent_issues.id AND f.applied = 0 ORDER BY f.id DESC LIMIT 1) WHERE status = 'open' AND id IN (SELECT issue_id FROM issue_fold_ledger WHERE applied = 0);
UPDATE issue_triage SET triage_state = 'closed', triaged_at = datetime('now'), close_evidence = (SELECT f.evidence FROM issue_fold_ledger f WHERE f.issue_id = issue_triage.issue_id AND f.applied = 0 ORDER BY f.id DESC LIMIT 1) WHERE issue_id IN (SELECT f.issue_id FROM issue_fold_ledger f JOIN agent_issues a ON a.id = f.issue_id WHERE f.applied = 0 AND a.status = 'open');
UPDATE agent_issues SET status = 'closed', updated_at = CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000 WHERE status = 'open' AND id IN (SELECT f.issue_id FROM issue_fold_ledger f JOIN issue_triage t ON t.issue_id = f.issue_id WHERE f.applied = 0 AND t.triage_state = 'closed' AND t.close_evidence = f.evidence);
UPDATE issue_fold_ledger SET applied = 1, applied_at = datetime('now') WHERE applied = 0 AND (SELECT a.status FROM agent_issues a WHERE a.id = issue_fold_ledger.issue_id) <> 'open';

-- 4. The hourly workflow: the same eleven statements as 1 and 3 (offline suite migrations/issue-hygiene.test.mjs holds the two equal)
INSERT INTO fleet_tasks (id, name, type, definition, timeout_ms, retries, version, enabled, updated_at)
VALUES ('issue-meta-fold', 'ISSUE-HYGIENE-1: close a ticket about a record when that record is resolved (probe-needed target closed, merge refused but merged, code loop done, ledger row resolved, owner task for a closed issue, repeated owner prompt)', 'workflow', '{"steps":[{"type":"sql","db":"AUDIT","sql":"INSERT INTO issue_fold_ledger (issue_id, rule, successor_id, evidence, agent_status, agent_updated_at, agent_close_channel, triage_state, triage_close_evidence, triage_reopened_count, triage_triaged_at, contract_class, contract_status, contract_last_verdict, contract_last_attempt_at) SELECT m.id, ''probe-needed-target-not-open'', x.id, ''moot: issue '' || x.id || '' is '' || x.status || '' ('' || substr(x.title, 1, 80) || ''): the probe this issue asked for belongs to a target that no longer needs one, so the to-do outlived its subject. ISSUE-HYGIENE-1 '' || strftime(''%Y-%m-%d'', ''now''), m.status, m.updated_at, m.close_channel, t.triage_state, t.close_evidence, t.reopened_count, t.triaged_at, c.class, c.status, c.last_verdict, c.last_attempt_at FROM agent_issues m JOIN issue_triage t ON t.issue_id = m.id LEFT JOIN remediation_contracts c ON c.class = ''issue-'' || m.id JOIN agent_issues x ON x.id = CAST(substr(m.title, 23) AS INTEGER) WHERE m.status = ''open'' AND m.title GLOB ''PROBE-NEEDED-1: issue-[0-9]*'' AND x.status <> ''open'' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_fold_ledger f WHERE f.issue_id = m.id AND f.applied = 0) ORDER BY m.id LIMIT 200"},{"type":"sql","db":"AUDIT","sql":"INSERT INTO issue_fold_ledger (issue_id, rule, successor_id, evidence, agent_status, agent_updated_at, agent_close_channel, triage_state, triage_close_evidence, triage_reopened_count, triage_triaged_at, contract_class, contract_status, contract_last_verdict, contract_last_attempt_at) SELECT m.id, ''code-merge-refused-task-merged'', NULL, ''moot: code task '' || k.id || '' is merged (code_tasks.status, last updated '' || COALESCE(k.updated_at, ''?'') || ''), so the merge refusal this issue recorded no longer holds. ISSUE-HYGIENE-1 '' || strftime(''%Y-%m-%d'', ''now''), m.status, m.updated_at, m.close_channel, t.triage_state, t.close_evidence, t.reopened_count, t.triaged_at, c.class, c.status, c.last_verdict, c.last_attempt_at FROM agent_issues m JOIN issue_triage t ON t.issue_id = m.id LEFT JOIN remediation_contracts c ON c.class = ''issue-'' || m.id JOIN code_tasks k ON k.id = substr(m.title, 33, instr(substr(m.title, 33) || '' '', '' '') - 1) WHERE m.status = ''open'' AND m.title LIKE ''CODE-MERGE-REFUSED-1: code task ct_%'' AND k.status = ''merged'' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_fold_ledger f WHERE f.issue_id = m.id AND f.applied = 0) ORDER BY m.id LIMIT 200"},{"type":"sql","db":"AUDIT","sql":"INSERT INTO issue_fold_ledger (issue_id, rule, successor_id, evidence, agent_status, agent_updated_at, agent_close_channel, triage_state, triage_close_evidence, triage_reopened_count, triage_triaged_at, contract_class, contract_status, contract_last_verdict, contract_last_attempt_at) SELECT m.id, ''code-loop-exhausted-dod-met'', r.id, ''moot: the definition of done of this issue (the task or a task that replaces it reaches ready_to_publish or later) is met: '' || CASE WHEN r.status IN (''closed'', ''resolved'') THEN ''issue '' || r.id || '' ('' || substr(r.title, 1, 70) || '') is '' || r.status ELSE ''a replacement task for issue '' || r.id || '' is merged or published'' END || ''. ISSUE-HYGIENE-1 '' || strftime(''%Y-%m-%d'', ''now''), m.status, m.updated_at, m.close_channel, t.triage_state, t.close_evidence, t.reopened_count, t.triaged_at, c.class, c.status, c.last_verdict, c.last_attempt_at FROM agent_issues m JOIN issue_triage t ON t.issue_id = m.id LEFT JOIN remediation_contracts c ON c.class = ''issue-'' || m.id JOIN code_tasks k ON k.id = substr(m.title, 24, instr(substr(m.title, 24) || '' '', '' '') - 1) JOIN agent_issues r ON r.id = CASE WHEN k.id LIKE ''ct_im%'' THEN CAST(substr(k.id, 6) AS INTEGER) WHEN k.goal LIKE ''[issue #%'' THEN CAST(substr(k.goal, 9) AS INTEGER) END WHERE m.status = ''open'' AND m.title LIKE ''CODE-LOOP-EXHAUSTED-1: ct_%'' AND (r.status IN (''closed'', ''resolved'') OR EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM code_tasks k2 WHERE k2.id <> k.id AND k2.status IN (''merged'', ''published'') AND (k2.id = ''ct_im'' || r.id OR instr(k2.goal, ''[issue #'' || r.id || '']'') > 0))) AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_fold_ledger f WHERE f.issue_id = m.id AND f.applied = 0) ORDER BY m.id LIMIT 200"},{"type":"sql","db":"AUDIT","sql":"INSERT INTO issue_fold_ledger (issue_id, rule, successor_id, evidence, agent_status, agent_updated_at, agent_close_channel, triage_state, triage_close_evidence, triage_reopened_count, triage_triaged_at, contract_class, contract_status, contract_last_verdict, contract_last_attempt_at) SELECT m.id, ''ledger-escalation-resolved'', NULL, ''moot: the filing loop resolved its own ledger row (fingerprint '' || (SELECT l.fingerprint FROM issue_ledger l WHERE (l.title = m.title OR (m.title LIKE ''[self-heal] tool %'' AND l.title LIKE ''[self-heal] tool %'' AND substr(l.title, 18, instr(substr(l.title, 18) || '' '', '' '') - 1) = substr(m.title, 18, instr(substr(m.title, 18) || '' '', '' '') - 1))) AND l.status IN (''resolved'', ''muted'') ORDER BY l.last_seen DESC LIMIT 1) || '', last seen '' || (SELECT l.last_seen FROM issue_ledger l WHERE (l.title = m.title OR (m.title LIKE ''[self-heal] tool %'' AND l.title LIKE ''[self-heal] tool %'' AND substr(l.title, 18, instr(substr(l.title, 18) || '' '', '' '') - 1) = substr(m.title, 18, instr(substr(m.title, 18) || '' '', '' '') - 1))) AND l.status IN (''resolved'', ''muted'') ORDER BY l.last_seen DESC LIMIT 1) || '') and no open ledger row remains for it, so this escalation copy has nothing left to track. ISSUE-HYGIENE-1 '' || strftime(''%Y-%m-%d'', ''now''), m.status, m.updated_at, m.close_channel, t.triage_state, t.close_evidence, t.reopened_count, t.triaged_at, c.class, c.status, c.last_verdict, c.last_attempt_at FROM agent_issues m JOIN issue_triage t ON t.issue_id = m.id LEFT JOIN remediation_contracts c ON c.class = ''issue-'' || m.id WHERE m.status = ''open'' AND instr(COALESCE(m.description, ''''), ''AUTO-ESCALATION from evReview'') = 1 AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_ledger l WHERE (l.title = m.title OR (m.title LIKE ''[self-heal] tool %'' AND l.title LIKE ''[self-heal] tool %'' AND substr(l.title, 18, instr(substr(l.title, 18) || '' '', '' '') - 1) = substr(m.title, 18, instr(substr(m.title, 18) || '' '', '' '') - 1))) AND l.status IN (''resolved'', ''muted'')) AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_ledger l WHERE (l.title = m.title OR (m.title LIKE ''[self-heal] tool %'' AND l.title LIKE ''[self-heal] tool %'' AND substr(l.title, 18, instr(substr(l.title, 18) || '' '', '' '') - 1) = substr(m.title, 18, instr(substr(m.title, 18) || '' '', '' '') - 1))) AND l.status IN (''open'', ''acknowledged'')) AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_fold_ledger f WHERE f.issue_id = m.id AND f.applied = 0) ORDER BY m.id LIMIT 200"},{"type":"sql","db":"AUDIT","sql":"INSERT INTO issue_fold_ledger (issue_id, rule, successor_id, evidence, agent_status, agent_updated_at, agent_close_channel, triage_state, triage_close_evidence, triage_reopened_count, triage_triaged_at, contract_class, contract_status, contract_last_verdict, contract_last_attempt_at) SELECT m.id, ''owner-task-names-closed-issue'', r.id, ''moot: the task asks for the fix of issue '' || r.id || '' ('' || substr(r.title, 1, 70) || ''), which is '' || r.status || '' with close evidence: '' || substr(COALESCE((SELECT x.close_evidence FROM issue_triage x WHERE x.issue_id = r.id), ''(none recorded)''), 1, 160) || '' ISSUE-HYGIENE-1 '' || strftime(''%Y-%m-%d'', ''now''), m.status, m.updated_at, m.close_channel, t.triage_state, t.close_evidence, t.reopened_count, t.triaged_at, c.class, c.status, c.last_verdict, c.last_attempt_at FROM agent_issues m JOIN issue_triage t ON t.issue_id = m.id LEFT JOIN remediation_contracts c ON c.class = ''issue-'' || m.id JOIN agent_issues r ON r.id = CAST(substr(m.title, instr(m.title, ''(issue #'') + 8) AS INTEGER) WHERE m.status = ''open'' AND m.source = ''qnfo-fleet-dashboard:owner-request'' AND m.title LIKE ''OWNER-TASK-op-%'' AND instr(m.title, ''(issue #'') > 0 AND r.id <> m.id AND r.status IN (''closed'', ''resolved'') AND instr(m.title, substr(r.title, 1, MIN(30, instr(r.title || '':'', '':'') - 1))) > 0 AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_fold_ledger f WHERE f.issue_id = m.id AND f.applied = 0) ORDER BY m.id LIMIT 200"},{"type":"sql","db":"AUDIT","sql":"INSERT INTO issue_fold_ledger (issue_id, rule, successor_id, evidence, agent_status, agent_updated_at, agent_close_channel, triage_state, triage_close_evidence, triage_reopened_count, triage_triaged_at, contract_class, contract_status, contract_last_verdict, contract_last_attempt_at) SELECT m.id, ''owner-prompt-twin'', s.id, ''superseded by '' || s.id || '' ('' || substr(s.title, 1, 100) || '', open): the same owner prompt filed again, because the dashboard intake dedupes by whole title and every title carries its own op id. The older ticket carries the work. ISSUE-HYGIENE-1 '' || strftime(''%Y-%m-%d'', ''now''), m.status, m.updated_at, m.close_channel, t.triage_state, t.close_evidence, t.reopened_count, t.triaged_at, c.class, c.status, c.last_verdict, c.last_attempt_at FROM agent_issues m JOIN issue_triage t ON t.issue_id = m.id LEFT JOIN remediation_contracts c ON c.class = ''issue-'' || m.id JOIN agent_issues s ON s.id = (SELECT MIN(o.id) FROM agent_issues o WHERE o.status = ''open'' AND o.id < m.id AND o.source = m.source AND (o.title LIKE ''OWNER-TASK-op-%'' OR o.title LIKE ''OWNER-NOTE-%'') AND lower(trim(substr(o.title, instr(o.title, '': '') + 2))) = lower(trim(substr(m.title, instr(m.title, '': '') + 2)))) WHERE m.status = ''open'' AND m.source = ''qnfo-fleet-dashboard:owner-request'' AND (m.title LIKE ''OWNER-TASK-op-%'' OR m.title LIKE ''OWNER-NOTE-%'') AND instr(m.title, '': '') > 0 AND length(lower(trim(substr(m.title, instr(m.title, '': '') + 2)))) >= 20 AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_fold_ledger f WHERE f.issue_id = m.id AND f.applied = 0) ORDER BY m.id LIMIT 200"},{"type":"sql","db":"AUDIT","sql":"UPDATE remediation_contracts SET status = ''superseded'', last_verdict = ''superseded:closure-superseded (ISSUE-HYGIENE-1)'', last_attempt_at = datetime(''now'') WHERE class IN (SELECT f.contract_class FROM issue_fold_ledger f WHERE f.applied = 0 AND f.contract_class IS NOT NULL) AND status IN (''monitoring'', ''escalated'', ''active'', ''holding'', ''needs-machine-probe'', ''probe-review-refused'')"},{"type":"sql","db":"AUDIT","sql":"UPDATE agent_issues SET close_channel = ''workflow:ISSUE-HYGIENE-1 '' || (SELECT f.rule FROM issue_fold_ledger f WHERE f.issue_id = agent_issues.id AND f.applied = 0 ORDER BY f.id DESC LIMIT 1) WHERE status = ''open'' AND id IN (SELECT issue_id FROM issue_fold_ledger WHERE applied = 0)"},{"type":"sql","db":"AUDIT","sql":"UPDATE issue_triage SET triage_state = ''closed'', triaged_at = datetime(''now''), close_evidence = (SELECT f.evidence FROM issue_fold_ledger f WHERE f.issue_id = issue_triage.issue_id AND f.applied = 0 ORDER BY f.id DESC LIMIT 1) WHERE issue_id IN (SELECT f.issue_id FROM issue_fold_ledger f JOIN agent_issues a ON a.id = f.issue_id WHERE f.applied = 0 AND a.status = ''open'')"},{"type":"sql","db":"AUDIT","sql":"UPDATE agent_issues SET status = ''closed'', updated_at = CAST(strftime(''%s'', ''now'') AS INTEGER) * 1000 WHERE status = ''open'' AND id IN (SELECT f.issue_id FROM issue_fold_ledger f JOIN issue_triage t ON t.issue_id = f.issue_id WHERE f.applied = 0 AND t.triage_state = ''closed'' AND t.close_evidence = f.evidence)"},{"type":"sql","db":"AUDIT","sql":"UPDATE issue_fold_ledger SET applied = 1, applied_at = datetime(''now'') WHERE applied = 0 AND (SELECT a.status FROM agent_issues a WHERE a.id = issue_fold_ledger.issue_id) <> ''open''"}]}', 120000, 1, 1, 1, datetime('now'))
ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, definition = excluded.definition, version = fleet_tasks.version + 1, enabled = 1, updated_at = excluded.updated_at;

INSERT INTO fleet_crons (name, cron_expr, task_id, enabled, timezone, updated_at)
VALUES ('issue-meta-fold-hourly', '20 * * * *', 'issue-meta-fold', 1, 'UTC', datetime('now'))
ON CONFLICT(name) DO UPDATE SET cron_expr = excluded.cron_expr, task_id = excluded.task_id, enabled = excluded.enabled, updated_at = excluded.updated_at;

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO failure_modes (fm_key, failure_mode, root_cause, remediation, detector, probe_class, first_seen, issue_id, trigger_condition, symptom, blast_radius) VALUES
 ('meta-issue-outlives-subject',
  'a ticket about another record (a probe to write, a merge refused, a code loop exhausted, a self-heal escalation, a repeated owner prompt) stays open after its subject is resolved or duplicated, so the open count carries tickets that track nothing',
  'the filers (REOPEN-LIVE-PATH-3, the merge runner, the code orchestrator, qnfo-observability evReview, the dashboard intake) open a ticket and none of them closes it when the subject resolves; PROBE-REVIEW-1 puts a closed-target PROBE-NEEDED-1 probe in probe-review-refused, which takes it out of the auto-close path; evReview keys by a ledger title that embeds a changing count; the intake dedupes by a title that carries a unique op id',
  'ISSUE-HYGIENE-1: issue_fold_ledger and the hourly workflow issue-meta-fold close each such ticket with the fact that resolved it (moot or superseded by, nothing deleted, nothing wontfix); evReview dedupes by fingerprint; fm-meta-issue-outlives-subject reads a stalled workflow or a ledger row not applied within two hours; no trigger is added to agent_issues',
  'the issue-meta-fold workflow fired in the last 150 minutes and no issue_fold_ledger row is pending for over 2 hours', 'fm-meta-issue-outlives-subject', '2026-10-26', NULL,
  'a subject resolves while its ticket stays open, or the same prompt or ledger row is filed under a new title',
  'open_agent_issues counts tickets that track nothing (2026-10-26: 57 of 438), the GitHub list repeats them, issue_drain_ratio_24h stays under 1.5',
  'the owner reading the open-issue count, METRIC-TRIGGER tickets on open_agent_issues, issues_over_24h_no_doer');

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO remediation_contracts (class, issue_id, precondition, action, verify_probe, verify_transport, max_attempts, escalate_to, expected_cadence_h, status, module) VALUES
 ('fm-meta-issue-outlives-subject', NULL, 'ISSUE-HYGIENE-1', 'failure-mode detector',
  'SELECT ''0'' AS expected, CAST((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM issue_fold_ledger WHERE applied = 0 AND created_at < datetime(''now'', ''-2 hours'')) + (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM fleet_crons WHERE name = ''issue-meta-fold-hourly'' AND (enabled = 0 OR last_fired IS NULL OR replace(substr(last_fired, 1, 19), ''T'', '' '') < datetime(''now'', ''-150 minutes''))) AS TEXT) AS observed',
  'd1-query', 3, 'qnfo-fleet-control', 1, 'active', 'failure-mode');

INSERT INTO decision_log (actor, assumption, action, evidence, outcome, blast_radius, rollback_path, capability_gain, predicted_outcome, reach_gain, surfaces_tested)
SELECT 'claude-code-session_015kWmGuAq2fNuvzu4MrD7x3',
  'a ticket about a record has no work of its own: when the record is resolved (target closed, task merged, definition of done met, ledger row resolved) or the same prompt was filed again, closing it with that fact loses nothing, and the carrying ticket keeps the work',
  'ISSUE-HYGIENE-1: issue_fold_ledger saves the before-state, then closes with evidence the tickets that outlived their subject or duplicate an older open ticket (probe-needed target closed, merge refused but merged, code-loop definition of done met, self-heal ledger row resolved, owner task for a closed issue, repeated owner prompt, three merged-PR repair requests, seven same-objective pairs); the six live-state rules run hourly as the workflow issue-meta-fold',
  'd1 qnfo-audit 2026-10-26, each rule dry-run as a SELECT before this file: 5 + 10 + 7 + 3 + 10 + 5 + 10 + 7 = 57 issues; PRs 3931 3935 3941 merged 2026-10-25 (GitHub read); ledger rows resolved (selfheal:eb999bb1, 9e71df71, 3ddf9c26, 85ef1588); code_tasks status merged for the ten refused tasks; agent_issues 100345 100560 100618 closed with verified close evidence; 24 live agent_issues triggers and the D1 10-level limit (no trigger added)',
  'migration merged; workflow issue-meta-fold registered',
  'at most 57 agent_issues rows closed with evidence on the first apply (each with an issue_lifecycle row), their GitHub mirrors close through TRACKER-SYNC-1; every ticket that carries work stays open',
  'issue_fold_ledger holds the before-state of each close; the Rollback header reopens the issues and restores triage and contracts (this decision row stays: decision_log is append-only); UPDATE fleet_crons SET enabled = 0 stops the workflow',
  'tickets about a record close within the hour of the record resolving',
  'open_agent_issues <= 381 right after the apply and no PROBE-NEEDED-1 or CODE-MERGE-REFUSED-1 older than 2 hours names a resolved subject',
  'none',
  'd1:qnfo-audit agent_issues, issue_triage, remediation_contracts, code_tasks, issue_ledger, v_metric_trigger_state, sqlite_master (SELECT only, each rule); github PR reads for 3931 3935 3941; offline node:sqlite suite migrations/issue-hygiene.test.mjs replays the live close triggers, applies the file twice and runs its Rollback'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM decision_log WHERE instr(action, 'ISSUE-HYGIENE-1:') = 1);
